  "notes": "Built directly from the archived 2025-26 bulletin's own 'Linguistics, B.A. at University Park Campus' Suggested Academic Plan and Program Requirements tabs (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/undergraduate/colleges/liberal-arts/linguistics-ba/) -- fetched and checked row-by-row (not just WebFetch-summarized) against LING-2026.json's own semesters array. Confirmed byte-identical to LING-2026.json in every respect: same Suggested Academic Plan table (same courses, same credits, same row order, including the 'LA 283' Second-Year Liberal Arts Seminar appearing twice at 1.5cr each in Semester 1 and Semester 4, and the same Semester-1 3cr source-reconciliation gap -- 17.5cr stated vs 14.5cr itemized -- that LING-2026.json already documents), same Program Requirements pool (Prescribed Courses LING 100/402/404/449; the 3-way LING 405/448/APLNG 200 'Linguistics Social Science Requirement' pool; the FR 316/417/418/419, GER 412/430, LATIN 450W, LING 493, SPAN 314/315N/316/418 'Non-English Linguistics Course' pool, LATIN 450W excluded for the same no-latin_catalog.json reason as 2026), and the same separate 'Linguistics, B.A. at Commonwealth Campuses' plan (121.5cr total, one LA 283 occurrence instead of two) confirming this is the first catalog edition where UP and Commonwealth Campuses split into two suggested-plan tables (2022-2024 published one combined table; see LING-2022/2023/2024.json). No real curriculum differences found for this year -- reused LING-2026.json's semesters array verbatim (only catalog_year/source changed). Entrance to major requires a 2.00 GPA and third-semester classification, not modeled directly. Real prereq-fix fallout: STAT 200 requires MATH 21 (which itself requires MATH 4 and MATH 3) -- a full remedial placement chain never otherwise scheduled in this plan; confirmed this prereq text is unchanged across the whole 2022-2026 span (see LING-2022.json's citation of the archived 2022-23 STAT course-description page), so the same STAT 200/STAT 100 fallback applies; the item resolves to STAT 100 (3cr instead of 4cr) rather than chasing the remedial chain. Generic B.A. Field/Gen Ed/Elective pools, and the still-open 'LING 4XX Course'/'Related Area Course' slots, modeled generically for the same reasons documented in LING-2026.json's own notes.",
